export anchor DispatchConsoleStyle:
    number: 350
    screen: TeamChat
    name: Dispatch console
    idea: The chat as an emergency dispatch screen, where channels wait in a prioritised call queue, messages land as timestamped log entries in ruled columns, and people are units marked available, away or offline.
    base: dark
    palette:
        page: #080d14, the page, fields and the style sheet
        panel: #0f1824, the queue, log and units panes
        head: #16233a, pane headers, the status strip and function keys
        grid: #253850, every rule and the 1px gaps between panes
        ink: #e3ecf7, text
        muted: #9fb1c7, column heads, states and CLEAR
        cyan: #38bdf8, the open line, times, Send and focus, with text #03202f
        p1: #ff7a7a, the P1 mention tag on #3a1218
        p2: #ffc04d, the P2 unread tag, away and the live strip on #33260a
        ok: #4ade80, available
    type:
        A sans, Inter, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Arial, at 13px with
        tabular numbers, and a monospace, ui-monospace, JetBrains Mono,
        DejaVu Sans Mono, Menlo, Consolas, for times, tags and headers.
        Pane headers 11px mono bold capitals tracked 0.12em, channel names
        14px at 650, message text 14px, the clock 16px mono.
    layout:
        A full width console. A status strip with a 2px cyan rule below
        reads BRIGHTWORK CHAT DISPATCH, Console 2, Operator Mara Okafor,
        Channel design-crit, and a large clock on the right. An amber live
        strip below reads Live, Priya is typing, with a pulse icon. Three
        panes, 300px queue, the log and 230px units, divided by 1px gaps
        that show the grid colour. Call queue lists channels by priority,
        each row with a 4px left bar and a tag, billing-war-room first with
        a red diamond P1 tag and 1 mention for you, then mobile-release
        with an amber triangle P2 tag and 4 unread waiting, then
        design-crit with a solid cyan dot OPEN tag and Active on this
        console, then general and random with outlined dash CLEAR tags and
        Nothing waiting. The log has column heads Time, Unit, Entry and
        Links, and ruled zebra rows with the time in cyan mono, a small
        initials code and the name, the text, and a links column. Aiko's
        row is selected with a cyan inset bar and its links read Thread, 3
        replies, Thumbs up x3 and Eyes x1. The image is a bordered chip,
        IMG and the filename, with Attachment, image in links. Units lists
        people with a full square and AVAILABLE, a half filled square and
        AWAY, an empty square and OFFLINE. Under the panes a New entry row
        holds the field and F1 Attach, F2 Emoji and a cyan F12 Send key.
        Below 1080px units move under, below 720px rows stack with the
        time on the left.
    spacing: A 4px unit. 8px by 12px cells, 1px gaps between panes.
    density: High. Queue, log and units all visible at once, every row ruled.
    corners: 2px on keys, fields and tags. Panes are square.
    borders: 1px grid rules, a 4px left bar coloured by priority and a 2px cyan rule under the strip.
    shadows: None. Selection is an inset 3px cyan bar.
    icons: Shape codes before every state, diamond P1, triangle P2, dot OPEN, dash CLEAR, and full, half or empty squares for units.
    focus: A 2px cyan outline with a 4px deep cyan halo.
    tone: Operational shorthand, such as Call queue, 4 unread waiting, Units, New entry and F12 Send.
